{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43202 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 5H-Indolo[3,2-B]Quinolin-11(10H)-One may interact with HPAC through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is linked to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, and also to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by 5-Oxobrucine. Both of these intermediates ultimately target HPAC. While the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear, the evidence points to a potential role of the drug in modulating metabolic pathways that lead to HPAC engagement. The overlapping targets and the presence of multiple intermediates suggest a possible regulatory or metabolic interaction, though the precise nature of the relationship remains to be elucidated.",
